[{:db/id "q-130620/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" :answer/id #uuid "3f4bc631-772a-5623-aeea-3baa1881ddd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130620/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "9778c2d8-4e24-566a-959f-c9946b50f0e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130620/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "e529cc70-407c-58e6-8d72-98df69c51ed0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130620/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "cd19d113-9bdf-54fb-9de8-b7c25d11c33b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130620/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "e3a1db8f-8d05-5677-b494-1c75207587c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130620/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "acffd64e-aa01-595f-a2a3-489a6b759b61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130620/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer-field/choices ["q-130620/selection/2b998a440c758092569557828849b9a2d05282247ea8a11a5727b6cadcbcb080" "q-130620/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-130620/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-130620/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-130620/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130620" :question/id #uuid "2d10f730-d88e-5867-be87-5a616a4cee43" :question/math-academy-id "q-130620" :question/problem "Find the possible values of the constant $x$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & -x\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." :question/worked-solution "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & -x\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ x & -x\\end{aligned}|+8|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-x+2)-5(-x-2x)+8(-1-x) \\\\  & =-3x+6+15x-8-8x \\\\  & =4x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130620/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130620"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-1778"] :question/problem "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{120}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={120}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{120}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{120}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-114251/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" :answer/id #uuid "cefdca8f-3077-51dd-81ef-397321227aa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114251/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "478d2baa-dfdb-5f7c-a968-32c9a381c1fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114251/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "644de2b3-6ce8-5b18-a2e4-a066efcf714d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114251/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "c8667878-e56e-5cb6-a96e-d410319c78cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114251/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "3333da21-a267-50fd-983d-00e50c8d5023" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114251/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bac6883d-4ab0-5dbd-ab9a-f112e4fbc14f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114251/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer-field/choices ["q-114251/selection/e53026d2e72b5a9665afb169ba986753fff36dfc4557e460320cb8d9594cece8" "q-114251/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-114251/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-114251/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-114251/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114251" :question/id #uuid "26d3b422-7b5a-59f6-92d8-0b2ae0c592e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114251" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21}=$" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=-1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[{x}^{2}+2x+1]}^{′}}{{[({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{2x+2}{4x({x}^{2}-4)-12} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{x+1}{2x({x}^{2}-4)-6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{x+1}{2x({x}^{2}-4)-6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[x+1]}^{′}}{{[2x({x}^{2}-4)-6]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{1}{6{x}^{2}-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6(-1)^{2}-8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114251/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a41d750-ffd9-5226-9bd7-b763575870c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114251"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123765/selection/434e5b9ed40adaf3ca2255268857c0c63681f364c2d21459ddbc2c544571b271" :answer/id #uuid "a454308d-8289-5655-9cc0-497565c7d239" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge -4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123765/selection/3cfc233d457edbec6b6deb35df070179afd90e6508c5585cd03e094cf600a715" :answer/id #uuid "b0db4239-64cb-5a18-90b4-cda5ea98a83b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123765/selection/b53bb0b24df3185c46f00d0fee587789db035759ea08279846091614b80a8c75" :answer/id #uuid "5626e6f4-2621-5391-a65b-da14e54a1b